---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const title = "\"It's like Goldilocks:\" Bespoke Slides for Fluctuating Audience Access Needs";
---
<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p class="meta">My take on the paper.</p>

  <div class="paper">
    <p>
      The author highlights the effect of power dynamics in accessibility for people with diverse disabilities daily and lack of equity on several levels, failure of guidelines resulting in API limitations. The inclusion of presenters in methodology is essential for achieving equal access and spreading awareness about the diversity of the viewers.
    </p>

    <p>
      Providing the presentation before was a great step in addition to coming up with a framework and a tool. The participants, as well as the presenters, lack trust in AI modifying the slide as per the "participant" choice, which is valid. This also takes away the control from the participants and the presenters. The paper not only highlights the diversity among the viewers that is often overlooked, but also the fluctuations that occur according to the time of day, the surrounding environment, etc.
    </p>

    <p>
      In addition to the framework suggested in the paper, I would like to suggest a tool and framework for both presenters and viewers. And not just relying on the tool, which has to be changed by the viewers.
    </p>

    <p>My suggested framework:</p>

    <p>
      Presenter's POV:<br />
      |__________Tool that implemented universal design for viewers with feedback loop from the viewers<br />
      |_____________Suggests changes for font ratio, background, with options of colour<br />
      __________________________visible to the user, guide to resources for accessibility
    </p>

    <p>
      Viewer's POV:<br />
      |___________Access to the original Presentation<br />
      |___________Tool with "split" slide deck option, "colour", "font"
    </p>

    <p>
      For future work, removing the power dynamics in school, workplace, and in other instances could be a great area for research and possible policy development.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
